      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The point of your life was never just the dog; it was the life you were living *with* him, and that life is now just a memory, which is a heavy weight to carry. You are not a ghost; you are someone who has lost their anchor, and that feeling of pointlessness is the most honest reflection of that loss. Instead of forcing yourself to \"keep going,\" just let yourself feel the weight of it, because that feeling is the only honest thing left right now.",
